  "notesHtml": "<ol>\n          <li>(a) Depreciation isn't a separate contra-asset column here &#x2014; it reduces the Equipment line directly in this template's Noncash Assets column.</li>\n          <li>(b) Supplies used = $17,250 &#x2212; $5,100 = $12,150.</li>\n          <li>(c) A pure accrual: liability up, expense up, no cash movement.</li>\n          <li>(d) One of four periods elapsed: $14,000 &#x00f7; 4 = $3,500.</li>\n          <li>(e) Nine of twelve months earned: 9/12 &#x00d7; $8,232 = $6,174. This is the one row where Revenue is recognized directly (insurance premium revenue), not just an expense.</li>\n          <li>(f) Another plain accrual: liability up, expense up.</li>\n          <li>(g) Interest earned but not received increases a receivable and Interest Income &#x2014; this list does have \"Instrst Rec\" as an option, unlike U3-Q1's list.</li>\n        </ol>\n        <button class=\"answer-toggle\" aria-expanded=\"false\">Answer <span class=\"chev\">&#x2304;</span></button>\n        <div class=\"answer-reveal\">\n          <ol>\n            <li><span class=\"ans-part\">a.</span> Decrease Equipment (Noncash Assets) by $3,150; decrease Retained Earnings (Earned Capital) by $3,150; increase Depreciation Expense (Expenses) by $3,150; decrease Net Income by $3,150.</li>\n            <li><span class=\"ans-part\">b.</span> Decrease Supplies (Noncash Assets) by $12,150; decrease Retained Earnings by $12,150; increase Supplies Expense by $12,150; decrease Net Income by $12,150.</li>\n            <li><span class=\"ans-part\">c.</span> Increase Utilities Payable (Liabilities) by $1,940; decrease Retained Earnings by $1,940; increase Utilities Expense by $1,940; decrease Net Income by $1,940.</li>\n            <li><span class=\"ans-part\">d.</span> Decrease Prepaid Rent (Noncash Assets) by $3,500; decrease Retained Earnings by $3,500; increase Rent Expense by $3,500; decrease Net Income by $3,500.</li>\n            <li><span class=\"ans-part\">e.</span> Decrease Unearned Revenue (Liabilities) by $6,174; increase Retained Earnings by $6,174; increase Insurance Premium Revenue (Revenues) by $6,174; increase Net Income by $6,174.</li>\n            <li><span class=\"ans-part\">f.</span> Increase Wages Payable (Liabilities) by $4,215; decrease Retained Earnings by $4,215; increase Wages Expense by $4,215; decrease Net Income by $4,215.</li>\n            <li><span class=\"ans-part\">g.</span> Increase Interest Receivable (Noncash Assets) by $1,350; increase Retained Earnings by $1,350; increase Interest Income (Revenues) by $1,350; increase Net Income by $1,350.</li>\n          </ol>\n        </div>"
